WEBVTT

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:09.420
Well, looks like this is it, kid.
Now I got a truck to catch.

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:11.940
Wait! Wait! I had something for you.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:13.660
(HANK CHUCKLES)

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:17.740
-Tag.
-The tag. Right!

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:27.900
You know,
I think I'm gonna remember you.

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:32.740
Oh, you'll forget me in a heartbeat, kid.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.500
Three heartbeats.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.500
I'll have a hard time
forgetting you though.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:42.540
(EXHALES DEEPLY)

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:44.620
My parents are actually down there.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.220
Um...

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.420
You okay?

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:53.860
I'm ready.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:57.460
(CHUCKLING) Yeah, I think you are.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:58.780
Whoa!

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:01.700
(GRUNTS)

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:03.300
(PANTING)

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:04.620
Wow!

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.340
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.620
Where are they? Where are they?
Where are they? Okay. Okay.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:23.420
Pardon me. Oh. Hi. Hello. Have you
seen a mom and a dad without me?

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.340
Excuse me. Have you seen a couple?

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:26.620
-They're old like you.
-(GASPS)

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.340
Not old like you,
but older than you even.

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:30.460
Okay. Bye.

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:35.820
Hi. Do you know anyone who lost a kid
a long time ago that would be me?

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:39.100
I don't know how long ago exact--
Okay. You're in a hurry. (GRUNTS)

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:41.460
-Ho, ho! Watch where you're going.
-Oh sorry.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.380
(GASPS)

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:52.020
SIGOURNEY: It's our goal that every
animal we rescue and care for...

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:54.660
will eventually return home
to where they belong.

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:00.820
Shells.

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:04.980
And there we go.
Now, if you ever get lost, Dory...

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:06.900
You just follow the shells.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.500
Hey, look! Shells!

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:10.860
(GASPS)

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:14.860
(BABY DORY LAUGHING)

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:18.140
Follow the shells.

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:32.820
-Hey, I live there.
-Yes, yes indeed.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:36.340
(GASPS) My home. That's my home!

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:39.500
Mom! Dad!

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.700
Okay, kelpcake. Now count to ten.

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:47.220
One, two, three...

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:49.460
-(GASPS)
-BABY DORY: Four...

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:52.380
(VOCALIZING) You're welcome.

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:54.260
Who are you talking to, kelpcake?

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:56.180
My pipe pal, Destiny!

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:03.060
Mom? Dad?

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:13.940
Mommy loves purple shells.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.060
(GASPS)

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:17.460
(SINGING)

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.140
(JENNY CRYING)

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:25.580
-Mommy?
-What's going to happen to her?

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:27.500
There, there, Jenny.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.660
Oh no, don't cry, Mommy. Don't cry.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:33.860
Do you think she's-- That she can
make it on her own, Charlie?

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:36.900
Oh, honey. It'll be okay.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.420
Mommy loves purple shells.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:51.860
(INHALES SHARPLY)

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:53.220
-Dory!
-Dory?

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:54.980
-Dory!
-Mommy?

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:56.180
(SCREAMS)

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:59.060
-CHARLIE: Dory!
-Mommy! Daddy!

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:00.300
(GASPING)

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:03.660
My parents...

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:07.180
I... I lost them.

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:17.460
It was my fault.

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:20.140
-FEMALE CRAB: Where's your tag?
-Huh?

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:24.100
Your tag. It's missing.
That why you're not in quarantine?

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:25.380
-Quarantine?
-Yeah!

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:28.660
That's where they took all
the blue tangs. Isn't that right, Bill?

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:31.820
Yep. The blue tangs are getting
their own exhibit in Cleveland.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:35.140
Being shipped out on a truck
at the crack of dawn. Must be nice.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:37.620
What? No! No, my parents
are back in quarantine?

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:40.540
They're being shipped to Cleveland?
But I just got here!

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:42.380
I've got to get to them.
They don't know I'm here.

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:44.980
Don't worry,
it's easy to get to quarantine.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:46.820
You can just go through the pipes,
honey.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:51.740
Oh. Oh I can't do that.

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:54.980
-Why not?
-I'll forget where I'm going.

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:58.300
And I can't be somewhere
where I have nobody to help me.

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:01.340
-Well, then I guess you're stuck here.
-You're not helping, Bill.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.020
Just go in there if you want to.
You'll be fine.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.140
Oh boy.

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:13.660
Could you tell me how to get there?
Through the pipes?

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:17.820
Sure, honey. It's two lefts
and then a right. Simple.

